      "writtenOn": "2015-01-05T21:23:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that features that aren\u0027t registered with the intellij could lead to strange behavior. They\u0027ve commented out their logging in \"FeatureUsageTrackerImpl.java:183\" but it does seem to indicate that an unregistered feature is considered an error. So any feature we decide to track will take their error branch when using this standard tracker (because registry.getFeatureDescriptor (line 181) will return false).\n\nI\u0027m not sure they\u0027d want us to pollute their registry with feature ids (especially the cloud ones).  Even if we decide to register our features by implementing the extension ProductiviyFeaturesProvider for this, we\u0027d probably be sending extra non-jetbrains plugin usage data to jetbrains.\n\nWould it make more sense to call the method triggerUnregisteredFeatureUsed(....) or something?\nor triggerExternalFeatureUsed(....) ?",
      "parentUuid": "ce156d30_dfb31368",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 191,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 191,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "c36f9172a0855fc4136cc301f55977b92f8caef8",
